.TH cron 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cron \- run commands at set times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cron
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cron
puts itself into the background and runs the commands listed in
.B /usr/lib/crontab
at the times given there.  It wakes once a minute, and re-reads the
table whenever its modification time changes \- so an edit takes effect
by itself, with nothing to signal.
.SH THE TABLE
Each line has five time fields and then a command.  The fields are
minute, hour, day of month, month (1 to 12), and day of week (0 to 6
from Sunday).  Each is either a number, several numbers separated by
commas, or
.B *
for every value.  Everything after the fifth field is the command, run
by
.BR sh (1).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
0 3 * * * /bin/fsck -a /dev/hdb3
15,45 * * * * /root/poll.sh
0 0 * * 0 /root/weekly.sh
.fi
.SH NOTES
There is no table on this machine as shipped, and
.B cron
is not started by
.BR /etc/rc .
Create
.B /usr/lib/crontab
and run
.B cron
to use it.
.PP
There is no
.B crontab
command and no per-user table: one file, edited with an editor.
.PP
This is the V7
.BR cron .
Step values such as
.B */5
and named months are not understood, and neither are ranges with a
hyphen.  Commands run as uid 1, not as root.
.PP
Output from a command goes nowhere.  Redirect it to a file if you want
to see it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/crontab
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR at (1),
.BR sh (1),
.BR sleep (1)
